#
# Conformance case: transaction/trajectory-audit-concurrent (T4 serializability).
#
# The READ-ONLY trajectory audit over CONCURRENT trajectories. The world facts (input.nq)
# record two gmeow:ToolCall trajectories that SHARE one start state (logic:transitionFromState
# ex:s0). The left trajectory writes ex:sitX then reads ex:sitY; the right trajectory writes
# ex:sitY then reads ex:sitX — an opposing-order read/write conflict cycle. The native auditor
# (crates/logic/src/transaction/trajectory.rs) discovers the bound ToolCalls
# (logic:instantiatesSchema), groups them under their logic:properPartOf anchors, orders each
# trajectory by gmeow:atTime, right-folds each into a logic:SerialConjunction, and — because the
# two anchors share a start state — composes them into a logic:ConcurrentComposition.
#
# At materialization the audit derives the logic:ConcurrentHistory of that composition: it builds
# the conflict graph (logic:precedes edges) from the two legs' read/write footprints and runs the
# serializability classifier. The cross-dependency footprints cycle, so the audit flags a
# logic:SerializationAnomaly finding alongside the history — proving T4 (conflict-serializability)
# at the corpus level, mirroring the engine unit test
# concurrent_cross_dependency_trajectories_flag_a_serialization_anomaly.
#
# Unlike the single-trajectory case this run COMMITS (no logic:HypotheticalExecution): the question
# is serializability of the recorded concurrent history, not hypothetical goal-reachability.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this input.logic.ttl
# carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the projections need.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/transaction/trajectory-audit-concurrent/> .

# The compile-time reasoning contract selects the Evolution facet that classifies the audited
# transaction. logic:TransactionPathEvolution drives certification to the transaction-path
# decidability class (conflict-serializability; PTIME classification, not search). The recorded
# concurrent history COMMITS, so no logic:executionMode logic:HypotheticalExecution is declared.
ex:TransactionContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:evolution logic:TransactionPathEvolution .
